    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318-a1">

                <pb facs="0491" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg397"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Papini to
                            Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New Orleans, La.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The witnesses brought from Hahnville, La., declare under oath and in writing that
                    the three persons lynched at that place were not naturalized. Their names are
                    Lorenzo Salardino, Salvatore Arena, and Giuseppe Venturella.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Papini</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Italian Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
